-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---Input fields handle text inputs and trigger `ONCONTENTCHANGE` actions in response.
---
---They support multiple input, filter, and text visibility modes, allowing them to be used for any type of text inputs,
---from chat messages, to pins and passwords.
---
---Custom Visuals: Using custom or plugin-provided sprites is supported, however the provided sprite must represent a
---spritesheet containing all of the potential states in a vertical layout using the following order - `default`,
---`disabled`.
---@class ui.InputField : ui.Component
---@field content string Gets or sets the current contents of the input field. If the component is restricted, attempting to retrieve the contents will yield an empty string.
---@field contentQuantity integer? (Read-only) Attempts to convert the current contents into an integer and returns it if successful. Only usable with numeric and quantity input fields.
---@field visibility ui.TextContentVisibilityMode Identifies how text will be drawn for this input field.
---@field filterMode ui.InputFieldFilterMode Identifies how inputs will be filtered by this input field.
---@field maxLength integer (Read-only) The maximum number of characters that are allowed in this input field.
---@field inputMode ui.InputFieldKeyHandlingMode Identifies how inputs will be handled by this input field.
---@field emptyText string Text to be displayed while this input field is empty.
---@field caretColour Vector4 Colour used for the cursor.
---@field caretRGBA Long Hex-encoded red/green/blue/alpha colour code for the cursor.
---@field errorCaretColour Vector4 Colour used for the cursor when an error occurs.
---@field errorCaretRGBA Long Hex-encoded red/green/blue/alpha colour code used for the cursor when an error occurs.
---@field selectionHighlightColour Vector4 Colour used for the text selection overlay.
---@field selectionHighlightRGBA Long Hex-encoded red/green/blue/alpha colour code used for the text selection overlay.
---@field emptyTextColour Vector4 Colour used for the text displayed while the input field is empty.
---@field emptyTextRGBA Long Hex-encoded red/green/blue/alpha colour code used for the text displayed while the input field is empty.
---@field contentMargin ui.Margin (Modifiable Contents) Offsets used to determine the inner content area for this component.
---@field text ui.TextData (Modifiable Contents) Text properties used when displaying this input field. Note using `text.content` will not yield the actual contents of the input field, and you must instead use the `content` property present on the input field itself.
---@field containerSprite ui.SpriteData (Modifiable Contents) Sprite properties used for the background.
---@field scrollbar ui.ScrollBar (Modifiable Contents) Scroll bar proprties used when vertical scrolling is required.
ui.InputField = {}

---Creates a new input field on the specified parent.
---
---Warning: Creating a component can fail if there's already a component on that parent with the same category ID and
---dynamic ID, or if those are omitted and the application is unable to generate a valid ID for the component.
---@param parent ui.ComponentCollection Parent component to create this input field in.
---@param categoryID? integer Category ID used to identify this component. Defaults to the parent's category ID if not specified.
---@param dynamicID? integer Dynamic ID used to identify this component. Defaults to auto-incrementing from the parent's dynamic ID if not specified.
---@return ui.InputField # The newly created input field. The caller must set its layout and visual information afterwards.
function ui.InputField.new(parent, categoryID, dynamicID) end

---Sets text handling and content drawing properties for this input field.
---
---Warning: Setting any visibility mode other than `ui.TextContentVisibilityMode.VISIBLE` will automatically tag the
---component as restricted.
---
---Info: Attempting to call this on a restricted input field will fail.
---@param visibility ui.TextContentVisibilityMode How the contents should be displayed to the user.
---@param filter ui.InputFieldFilterMode How inputs should be filtered, if at all.
---@param maxLength integer The maximum number of characters allowed.
function ui.InputField:Setup(visibility, filter, maxLength) end

---Identifies what inputs will be handled by an InputField component.
---@enum ui.InputFieldKeyHandlingMode
ui.InputFieldKeyHandlingMode = {
    ---Handles all inputs.
    DEFAULT = 0,
    ---Ignores keyboard arrow key inputs.
    CHAT = 1,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `ui.InputFieldKeyHandlingMode.FromID(ui.InputFieldKeyHandlingMode.DEFAULT)` is `"DEFAULT"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function ui.InputFieldKeyHandlingMode.FromID(value) end

---Contains the available filter modes for filtering user inputs written to an InputField component.
---@enum ui.InputFieldFilterMode
ui.InputFieldFilterMode = {
    ---No filtering, all inputs allowed.
    NONE = 0,
    ---No symbol inputs allowed.
    ALPHANUMERIC = 1,
    ---Only numbers allowed.
    NUMERIC = 2,
    ---Only allows numbers and english quantity designators (eg. `1K` representing `1000`, `1M` representing `1000000`).
    QUANTITY = 3,
    ---Only numbers allowed, with the resulting number always being represented as a string.
    NUMBERS_AS_TEXT = 4,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `ui.InputFieldFilterMode.FromID(ui.InputFieldFilterMode.NONE)` is `"NONE"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function ui.InputFieldFilterMode.FromID(value) end

---Contains the potential result type for the most recent input action on an InputField component.
---
---Info: Consider carefully what's the appropriate response to each of these action results based on the context around
---each component. While `submit` indicates active intent by the user to finalise input and trigger a potential action,
---the other options do not represent that active intent by default, depending entirely instead on the context. For
---example:
---
---Info: Keep in mind `submitOnEscape` and `submitOnFocusLoss` only represent a potential submit request. For example,
---you may want to treat focus loss as a submit request for an InputField used as a search filter, but it wouldn't make
---sense to do so for the chat box.
---@enum ui.InputFieldActionResult
ui.InputFieldActionResult = {
    ---No recent input actions.
    NONE = -1,
    ---An error occurred during the latest input action.
    ERROR = 1,
    ---The InputField's contents have changed due to the latest input action.
    CONTENT_CHANGE = 0,
    ---The latest input action was a submit request, triggered by the user pressing the Enter key.
    SUBMIT = 2,
    ---The latest input action may be treated as a submit request, triggered by the user pressing the Esc key.
    SUBMIT_ON_ESCAPE = 3,
    ---The latest input action may be treated as a submit request, triggered by the InputField losing focus due to the user clicking elsewhere.
    SUBMIT_ON_FOCUS_LOSS = 4,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `ui.InputFieldActionResult.FromID(ui.InputFieldActionResult.NONE)` is `"NONE"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function ui.InputFieldActionResult.FromID(value) end

---Contains the visibility modes available for text in InputFields.
---@enum ui.TextContentVisibilityMode
ui.TextContentVisibilityMode = {
    ---Text is always visible.
    VISIBLE = 0,
    ---All text other than the last character is hidden, replaced by `*` characters.
    SHOW_LAST = 1,
    ---All text is replaced by `*` characters.
    HIDDEN = 2,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `ui.TextContentVisibilityMode.FromID(ui.TextContentVisibilityMode.VISIBLE)` is `"VISIBLE"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function ui.TextContentVisibilityMode.FromID(value) end
